{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"13 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,39.017,3.651,3.268,"CP Plus (Aditya Infotech)"],[13.889,14.731,39.202,2.373,2.124,"Record profit, but the cash has not arrived"],[13.889,20.845,52.951,1.809,1.634,"India’s certification rule has shut out Chinese-linked cameras since April 2025,"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"and CP Plus owner Aditya Infotech has gained most. H1 FY27 revenue rose"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"90% to ₹3,148 cr and pre-tax profit before a fire loss more than tripled to ₹477"],[13.889,25.177,52.936,1.809,1.634,"cr. The shares are up 177% this year, at 71x FY27E EPS. Yet the profit has not"],[13.889,26.621,52.967,1.809,1.634,"arrived as cash: operating cash flow was −₹67 cr in H1 and −₹26 cr since April"],[13.889,28.065,52.951,1.809,1.634,"2024, against ₹1,155 cr of pre-tax profit, as inventory climbed to ₹1,908 cr."],[13.889,29.509,52.216,1.809,1.634,"Without September’s ₹1,500 cr placement there would be net debt of c.₹200 cr."],[13.889,31.995,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Q2’s 17.6% EBITDA margin is not a run-rate, as management says. Gross"],[13.889,33.439,52.934,1.809,1.634,"margin has slipped for three quarters (31.8%, 30.8%, 30.0%) as low-cost chips"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"and memory are used up; the gain came from other expenses, 5.5% of revenue"],[13.889,36.328,52.931,1.809,1.634,"against 8.4% in Q1. At Q1’s ratio the margin was 14.7%. The 42% market share"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"also uses a wider market than the 45.4% quoted in May (FY26 is now 34%), and"],[13.889,39.216,52.934,1.809,1.634,"underlying Q2 PAT is nearer ₹211 cr than the ₹220 cr presented, which adds"],[13.889,40.684,52.964,1.809,1.634,"back the fire loss before its tax relief. Guidance implies H2 margins of 11.8-"],[13.889,42.128,52.951,1.809,1.634,"13.8%; we sit just above, with FY27E revenue of ₹6,898 cr and EPS of ₹58.0,"],[13.889,43.572,33.466,1.809,1.634,"then ₹71.5 and ₹87.3 (consensus ₹60.0 and ₹76.7)."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹2,810 averages two methods. A 49x P/E, midway between"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"today’s 61x and the 38x median of Dixon, Kaynes, Syrma, Amber, Havells and"],[13.889,48.946,52.964,1.809,1.634,"Polycab, on forward EPS of ₹83.4 gives ₹4,090. A ten-year DCF (12% cost of"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"equity, 5.5% terminal growth) plus cash gives ₹1,530, as working capital ties up"],[13.889,51.834,52.964,1.809,1.634,"22% of revenue. The price needs operating profit to grow 35% a year in FY30-"],[13.889,53.278,52.934,1.809,1.634,"36E; we assume 16% fading to 8%. If gross margin holds at 30.4% the target is"],[13.889,54.722,52.966,1.809,1.634,"₹3,100; if component prices unwind, ₹2,170. Rating: Underweight. Upside risk:"],[13.889,56.167,49.152,1.809,1.634,"recorder certification. Downside: new certified entrants, memory deflation."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,68.023,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,000"],[14.451,66.066,2.306,1.022,0.915,"2,000"],[14.451,64.109,2.306,1.022,0.915,"3,000"],[14.451,62.152,2.306,1.022,0.915,"4,000"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"5,000"],[18.306,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,68.717,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.346,69.888,3.827,1.275,1.111,"CP Plus ("],[22.176,69.914,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.789,69.888,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.873,69.888,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.566,71.048,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.803,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[29.998,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.048,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.114,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.095,72.114,3.363,1.387,1.209,"176.9%"],[24.547,72.114,2.597,1.387,1.209,"-5.7%"],[28.528